; pair-eta (product extensionality): ∀p. (mkpair (fst p) (snd p)) = p — proven by the PRODUCT ELIMINATOR.
;
; This is the first library proof to use `prodrec`, the single-constructor product eliminator. It is the
; canonical demonstration of WHY prodrec is needed: fst/snd applied to an ABSTRACT p are STUCK (fun 100/101
; only fire on a concrete (k 70 a b)), so no amount of rewriting proves the goal directly. prodrec eliminates
; p into its type's sole constructor (k 70 a b) — licensed by the (prod 70) declaration — after which fst
; fires to a and snd to b, collapsing the goal to (k 70 a b) = (k 70 a b), closed by refl.
;
; The pair is (data 70 2 0 0); fst = (fun 100 70 (v 0)), snd = (fun 101 70 (v 1)), matching the meaning
; route's USER_PRELUDE. This lemma is the extensionality principle the ℤ (difference-pair) signed-sum fold
; theorem builds on — splitting an abstract integer element into its (pos, neg) components.
(data 70 2 0 0)
(fun 100 70 (v 0)) (fun 101 70 (v 1))          ; fst(mkpair a b)=a ; snd(mkpair a b)=b
(prod 70)                                       ; 70 is its type's SOLE constructor -> licenses prodrec
(all p (= (k 70 (f 100 p) (f 101 p)) p))
(prodrec 70 p (= (k 70 (f 100 p) (f 101 p)) p)
  (gen a (gen b (refl (k 70 a b)))))
